{"format":1,"seq":182,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The jq-based readEvents change needed for proposal 4 is too big a scope expansion, so I'll skip it and leave it as a follow-up, scoping the PR to just proposals 1 and 3. Now I'm starting the implementation in a new module, imitated-calls.ts, checking how AgentMessage from pi-agent-core relates to TurnEndEvent's message type.\n\nI'm writing a detection function that checks whether an assistant message's last text block ends with the elided-calls placeholder line, bailing early if the content contains actual tool calls or isn't an array. I'm second-guessing whether models might embed the placeholder mid-text and keep writing afterward, or emit multiple placeholders, since the issue only specifies \"at the end of a turn\" -- the last-line check should handle the common case, but I want to consider edge cases like partial placeholder text.\n\nI'm drafting a warning message for when this happens: \"No tool ran\" because the model wrote a text record describing a call instead of actually invoking a tool. The renderer shows a collapsed banner summarizing this, with a secondary line noting whether Pit nudged the model to retry, storing a `continued` boolean and expanding to reveal the full message text when clicked. I'm now wiring this notice into the turn_end handler, pushing the warning entry into the event's entries and conditionally setting a continue flag if the model should be prompted to make the call again.\n\nI want the placeholder text to clearly signal \"record of a past call; writing it runs nothing\" rather than vaguer phrasing, placed right after the label so it's visible early. That also means the regex tests checking the placeholder format will need updating to match the new wording.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01JMykYQQj3aXD6FoaW2NBJj","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read durable callNote and list tests asserting elided-call placeholder text\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read, search } }) => {\n  const [d, t] = await Promise.all([\n    read(\"src/durable/context/edits.ts\", { offset: 55, limit: 45 }),\n    search(\"elided tool call\", { path: \"test\", contextLines: 0, limit: 60 }),\n  ]);\n  return { d: d.content, rev: (d as any).revision, t: (t as any).matches.map((m: any) => `${m.file}:${m.line}: ${m.text.trim()}`) };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1686,"cacheRead":68398,"cacheWrite":7592,"totalTokens":77678,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1435},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794997941127,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_c6c7nk3pyiveauvr34qirtih4bnstcjvmfjbztwxq2p3li4umfsq","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":18033,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":75,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":74}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":74,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":75,"tools":[76],"pending":[]},"on":[76],"policy":"allSettled"},"startedAt":1794997941110}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":76,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.tool","version":3,"input":{"kind":"model","assistant":75,"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01JMykYQQj3aXD6FoaW2NBJj"},"owner":74,"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"pending","checkpoint":{"phase":"call"}}}},{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"base","value":{"run":{"taskId":74,"inputs":[8],"turns":17,"first":7},"tools":[{"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01JMykYQQj3aXD6FoaW2NBJj","name":"typescript","taskId":76,"status":"pending"}]}}},{"type":"document.change","id":4,"content":{"version":1,"kind":"base","value":{"models":{"nvidia/aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude